README high-signal
    70	4. **Open in browser**:
    71	   Navigate to `http://localhost:5173`
    72	
    73	### Project Structure
    74	
    75	```
    76	diedrico/
    77	├── frontend/          # Vue 3 + TypeScript frontend application
    78	│   ├── src/
    79	│   │   ├── commands/     # Command pattern (undo/redo)
    80	│   │   ├── components/   # Vue components (UI)
    81	│   │   ├── domain/       # Core domain model (geometry)
    82	│   │   ├── services/     # Application services
    83	│   │   ├── stores/       # Pinia state management
    84	│   │   └── tools/        # Interactive construction tools
    85	│   └── tests/         # Unit, integration, and E2E tests
    86	├── backend/           # Express backend (optional, for future features)
    87	├── docs/              # Deployment and setup documentation
    88	└── specs/             # Complete feature specifications
    89	    └── 001-dihedral-learning-mvp/
    90	        ├── spec.md           # Functional requirements
    91	        ├── ui-spec.md        # UI/UX specifications
    92	        ├── data-model.md     # Architecture documentation
    93	        └── tasks.md          # Implementation task breakdown
    94	```
    95	
    96	## 🛠️ Development
    97	
    98	### Available Scripts
    99	
   100	**Frontend development**:
   101	```bash
   102	npm run dev              # Start Vite dev server
   103	npm run build            # Build for production
   104	npm run test             # Run unit tests
   105	npm run test:watch       # Run tests in watch mode
   106	npm run test:e2e         # Run Playwright E2E tests
   107	npm run lint             # Lint and fix code
   108	```
   109	
   110	**Full workspace**:
   111	```bash
   112	npm run dev              # Start frontend dev server
   113	npm test                 # Run all tests
   114	```
   115	
   116	### Technology Stack
   117	
   118	**Frontend**:
   119	- **Vue 3** with Composition API for reactive UI
   120	- **TypeScript** for type safety
   121	- **Pinia** for state management
   122	- **Three.js** for 3D visualization
   123	- **D3.js** for 2D geometric operations
   124	- **Vite** for fast development and builds
   125	- **Vitest** for unit testing
   126	- **Playwright** for E2E testing
   127	
   128	**Backend** (minimal, planned for future features):
   129	- **Express** for API endpoints
   130	- **TypeScript** for consistency
   131	
   132	### Architecture Principles
   133	
   134	Diedrico follows strict architectural principles documented in [data-model.md](specs/001-dihedral-learning-mvp/data-model.md):
   135	
   136	1. **Parametric by default**: All geometric elements update when dependencies change
   137	2. **Explicit dependencies**: Process Tree tracks all element relationships
   138	3. **Command pattern**: All mutations through undoable commands
   139	4. **No implicit entities**: User must explicitly create all geometric objects
   140	5. **Plane-based organization**: 2D elements belong to specific projection planes
   141	6. **Type-safe domain model**: Comprehensive TypeScript types for all geometry
   142	
   143	### Key Concepts
   144	
   145	**Process Tree**: Every geometric element is created by an Action that tracks its inputs (dependencies). The Process Tree is the complete history of construction operations, enabling:
   146	- Parametric updates (change inputs, outputs recalculate)
   147	- Dependency visualization (see what depends on what)
   148	- Construction replay (understand the sequence)
   149	
   150	**Element Variations**: Each element type (Point, Line, Circle) has multiple construction methods. For example, points can be:
   151	- Free (positioned anywhere)
   152	- Intersection (where two elements cross)
   153	- On-element (constrained to a line or circle)
   154	- Transported (transferred between projection planes)
   155	
   156	**Realization**: The actual geometric representation (x, y coordinates, etc.) computed from an element's definition and dependencies. Realizations are cached and invalidated when dependencies change.
   157	
   158	## 📚 Documentation
